    13	\paragraph{Problem source.}
    14	The experimental apparatus contains a sealed air column (CA) in the inner
    15	cylinder.  Propylene glycol is introduced to h = 4.5 cm so the air volume is
    16	fixed.  Use the cylinder dimensions in Figure 17, ambient air density
    17	rho\_a = 1.12 kg/m\textasciicircum{}3, and the ideal-gas law P*V = n*R*T.  The outer-cylinder
    18	water bath is heated while pressure and temperature are recorded.
    19	
    20	Current subquestion:
    21	Determine the constant-volume thermal pressure coefficient beta\_0 = (1/P\_0)*(Delta P/Delta T).
    22	
